{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/k8q4ei","slideIndex":0,"text":"Based on ClinSync implementation: backend/routers/doctor.py (patient scope, order validation, cancellation); backend/routers/technician.py (assigned technician, sample state, duplicate sample/run checks, rejection and rerun); backend/routers/pathologist.py (review access, reasons, release); backend/lab_workflow.py (six displayed stages); frontend/src/api/client.ts (API errors). Received means technician assignment in the current application. Cancellation is permitted for Ordered/Assigned orders with no analysis results or released reports and no sample processing. Rejection does not automatically cancel. Key successful actions have audit records; the application does not provide a general integration failure log or message resend console. The analyser is simulated in the current implementation. The source was a screenshot; text and workflow were recreated as editable slide elements."}